<title>SWITZERLAND: ACI says Jan-Nov 1996 world air cargo up 6.3 pct.</title>
<headline>ACI says Jan-Nov 1996 world air cargo up 6.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Freight and mail traffic</p>
<p>handled by 473 airports around the world between January and November 1996, totalled 44,980,011 million tonnes, up 6.3 percent on the same period the previous year, said Geneva-based Airports Council International (ACI).</p>
<p>Cargo traffic in tonnes handled by airports in ACI's six geographical regions between January and November 1996, with percentage change on January-November 1995, in parentheses, was as follows:</p>
<p>				    Jan-Nov	   Percent Change</p>
<p>				     '96		on Jan-Nov '95</p>
<p>   Africa			397,357	     up   12.6</p>
<p>   Asia/Pacific	    9,257,344	     up    6.0</p>
<p>   Europe		    9,297,220	     up    4.5</p>
<p>   L.America/Carribean   1,106,018	     up    3.0</p>
<p>   Middle East	     1,435,272	     up   14.9</p>
<p>   North America	  23,486,800	     up    6.7</p>
<p>   Total		    44,980,011	     up    6.3</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
</text>
